<title>DEMOCRATIC REPUBLIC OF CONGO: Kabila leaves on first foreign trip as president.</title>
<headline>Kabila leaves on first foreign trip as president.</headline>
<dateline>KINSHASA 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Laurent Kabila set off on Sunday for this week's Organisation of African Unity summit in Zimbabwe, his first foreign outing as president of the Democratic Republic of Congo.</p>
<p>Four days after his inauguration as head of state and two weeks after his forces toppled veteran dictator Mobutu Sese Seko, Kabila left the capital Kinshasa aboard Mobutu's former presidential jet.</p>
<p>The summit runs from Monday to Wednesday.</p>
</text>
